Z||000000||fiero56||12-16-1999||08:39 PM||||Took the Fiero out for the first time in three weeks. The new clutch is pretty nice.  Although, it is going to take some getting used to. Pedal feel is a little heavier, not really a problem. Clutch starts to engage about a half inch lower than the stock one did, a little weird. The clutch doesn't "slap" engage. Before if I let off a little quickly, the car would really **** , this one engauges really softly, can't really "feel" it anymore. That also will take some time to get used to. The clutch set was a RAM heavy duty. <BR>Took the car out on 675 tonight, got it up to about 71mph, no shakes or anything, it felt pretty tight. All I have to do now, is figure out where 1/2 and inch of p. brake cable went to.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||12-16-1999||08:41 PM||||I just read my post, the forum astericked out j-e-r-k. So no-one tries to figure what thats supposed to mean, and can't get it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||12-16-1999||10:50 PM||||I forgot to mention the exhaust seems a bit louder, perfect for my taste. I can hear it with my window down, very low rumble. Plus, I had many people looking at my car again. That felt the best. After driving a minivan and sable for the last several weeks, my Fiero was a welcomed change. The shifter seems a little stiffer than before, I may need to re-route the cables and see what happens.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 12-16-1999).]||||reg||1
